// Ch4 C4-07, the optional side scene "The Ink" (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch04.md §4). The wake-shell
// wall after the feast (H15: 85 mm, 1.0 m, shallow depth of field; Ysolde's ink-guarded hand and brush
// on the shell, the oil lamp's pool, Rhen's hand holding it in the edge of frame; inserts on the two
// shells). The lamps have burned low, the tables are bare, the village has gone home. Reached after
// the dock, through the kneeling figure seen from the causeway-head path; going to Neme's door instead
// ends the night and the scene is gone. In the world the re-inking always happens (C4-08 shows it).
// Rules: no more than four Ysolde lines in a row; complete sentences, no contractions; she explains
// nothing about herself and does not give her name (C4-09 does), so her nameplate reads "The stranger"
// (M4-A2P-116 B1). She is cold because warmth would make
// it unbearable. "Once." is a widow's answer the player can't read yet (Ch13 pays it).
// Music: ysolde_theme (sketch). The chapter flow sets ch04_saw_ysolde_ink.
title: ch04_the_ink
location: ch04/haluna_wake
---
@letterbox on
@music ysolde_theme fade=2.0
@camera H15
@anim ysolde ink_shell
@sfx ink_brush at=ysolde
Ysolde as "The stranger" [cold]: Hold the lamp, if you are going to stand there. #line:ch04_ink_001
@anim rhen hold_lamp
Rhen [neutral]: What's wrong with the ink? #line:ch04_ink_002
Ysolde as "The stranger" [neutral]: They cut the name well. They inked it with fishing-ink, soot and oil. Salt lifts that in a season. #line:ch04_ink_003
Ysolde as "The stranger" [neutral]: Ansedran lacquer outlasts the stone it is in. #line:ch04_ink_004
Rhen [smile]: So you go round villages fixing other people's spelling. #line:ch04_ink_005
@wait 2.0
Rhen [neutral]: ...Sorry. #line:ch04_ink_006
@wait 1.5
@anim ysolde move_lamp
@sfx ink_brush at=ysolde
@wait 1.5
Rhen [sad]: That's her mother's. #line:ch04_ink_007
Ysolde as "The stranger" [neutral]: Yes. #line:ch04_ink_008
@wait 2.0
Rhen [neutral]: Have you done this before? #line:ch04_ink_009
@wait 1.0
Ysolde as "The stranger" [neutral]: Once. #line:ch04_ink_010
@wait 2.0
@anim ysolde cap_ink
Ysolde as "The stranger" [cold]: Go to sleep. The tide will not wait for anyone tomorrow. #line:ch04_ink_011
@mark ysolde wall_away walk
@wait 1.5
@letterbox off
@camera release
===
